  "all_ingredients_flat": "3 cups of whole wheat flour, 1.5 tsp active dry yeast, 1 cup of lukewarm soy milk, 1-2 cups of lukewarm water, 1/4 tsp black pepper powder, Finely chopped green chilies, 1 cup of finely chopped cilantro, 1.5 cups of finely chopped onion, 3-4 Tbsp finely chopped mint leaves, 2 sprigs of finely chopped curry leaves, 1 tsp cumin seeds, 1 tsp of salt, 1 tsp of date sugar or maple syrup, plant based milk of your choice",
  "instructions": "DOUGH: Mix and knead all the ingredients (except water and plant-based milk) in the Kitchen aid stand mixer. Add plant-based milk and water as needed to form a soft dough. Let it sit for almost 1hr covered with a damp cloth. Then softly knead the dough again and let it sit for another 1-2 hrs. BAKING: Transfer dough to a baking loaf pan. Lightly brush with plant based milk of your choice. Bake at 350F. I baked it for almost 45 mins. Check after 30 mins or so. Cool on a cooling rack before cutting into slices.",
  "cooking_methods": [
    "mix",
    "knead",
    "bake"
  ],
  "serving_suggestion": "",
  "notes": "For whole wheat flour, King Arthur brand was used. For lukewarm water, 1 cup was initially added, then maybe another quarter cup. Dry mint leaves were used. Baking time: check after 30 mins or so.",
